{"toolCallId":"call_96aed6889f8540f7bcd22a990a2c7557","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"+ FOLDER_NAMING: Folder name '001-recommend-level-quiet-flag' follows naming convention\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALUES: Frontmatter values are in the shared list\n+ SOURCE_TAGS: No [SOURCE:] path:line citations in research or review artifacts\n+ GREP_CONVENTION: Grep convention: 5 document(s) conform\n+ LEVEL_MATCH: Level consistent across all files (Level 3)\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT: children_ids matches the on-disk phase children\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY: children_ids entries all carry the packet's own identity\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE: graph-metadata.json shape validation passed\n+ METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY: metadata paths carry the scaffold marker; the packet is not filed yet\n+ DESCRIPTION_SHAPE: description.json shape validation passed\n+ NORMALIZER_LINT: No local normalizeScope*/getOptionalString declarations found outside allowed files\n+ SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY: Spec doc references, metadata, and handover targets resolve cleanly\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED: Canonical-save root-spec check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED: Canonical-save source-doc check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED: save_lineage is present for the refreshed graph metadata\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED: Packet identity normalization drift detected (soft detector)\n    - identity=scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n    - identity=zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS: Description and graph freshness stay within the canonical-save slack window\n+ CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS: Continuity freshness skipped: SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS is not enabled\n    - code:not_opted_in\n+ LINKS_VALID: All wikilinks under the system-spec-kit skill resolve\n\nSummary: Errors: 2  Warnings: 1\n\nRESULT: FAILED\n\nSome of these are recomputable from the repository:\n  preview  node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n  apply    add --apply\nEXIT=2\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"4aefb5","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_a3bf3523cc0a41188c7cc96d15ec7b86","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Repair Derived\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n'use strict';\n\n// Validation failures split into two kinds. Some are facts the repository\n// already knows and the document merely records wrongly: where a packet sits on\n// disk, what level it declares, whether its generated metadata still matches\n// its sources. Those can be recomputed and are what this repairs. The rest are\n// records of work someone did — evidence, verification results, decisions —\n// which cannot be derived from anything and must be written by whoever did the\n// work. Repairing only the first kind is the whole point: a tool that filled in\n// the second would make the gate green by making the packet lie.\n//\n// Dry by default; --apply writes. Everything --apply will write is named by the\n// dry run first, so the report is a faithful preview rather than a summary of\n// some of it. Idempotent, so a second run is a no-op.\n//\n// Exit: 0 = nothing left that this tool can repair; 1 = repairable work found\n// (dry run); 2 = something failed — a rejected argument, a packet whose report\n// could not be read, or a repair that did not land.\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nconst { execFile } = require('node:child_process');\nconst crypto = require('node:crypto');\nconst fs = require('node:fs');\nconst os = require('node:os');\nconst path = require('node:path');\nconst { promisify } = require('node:util');\n\nconst run = promisify(execFile);\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nconst REPO = process.cwd();\nconst VALIDATE = '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh';\nconst BACKFILL = '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.ts';\nconst TSX_LOADER = './.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs';\n\n// Each packet is validated by its own process and nothing is shared between\n// them, so the wall-clock cost is a scheduling problem rather than a real one.\n// Serially this walk takes hours, which is long enough that nobody runs it.\n//\n// Nearly all of a packet's cost is the validator's own rule subprocesses, so a\n// worker spends most of its life waiting on children rather than computing, and\n// the pool is worth pushing past the core count. Measured over a 181-packet\n// tree on 18 cores: 12 workers 57.7s, 16 → 49.1s, 24 → 45.9s, 32 → 45.6s. The\n// curve is flat past 24 and every worker holds a shell plus its node children,\n// so that is where the cap sits.\nconst WORKERS = Math.max(4, Math.min(24, Math.ceil(os.cpus().length * 1.5)));\n\n// A wedged validator would otherwise hold a worker — and so the whole run —\n// open forever. A packet takes about two seconds; five minutes is a hang.\nconst CHILD = { cwd: REPO, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024, timeout: 5 * 60 * 1000 };\n\n// Rules this tool can settle from repository state alone. Anything absent from\n// this list is reported and left alone, however mechanical it may look.\n//\n// The validator registry already classifies every rule, and this list is not\n// simply its structural category. Two deliberate differences, recorded here so\n// the next reader does not have to guess whether they were intended:\n//\n//   GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE is structural and included, because the re-derive\n//   rewrites the very file it makes assertions about.\n//\n//   SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY is classified as an authored-template rule and included\n//   anyway, because one of its two failure modes is a recorded location that\n//   has gone stale — recomputable — while the other is a reference to a file\n//   that no longer exists, which is not. Only the first is repaired; a packet\n//   failing solely on the second is reported as beyond this tool rather than\n//   passing silently.\nconst DERIVABLE = new Set([\n  'DESCRIPTION_SHAPE',\n  'GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY',\n  'GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT',\n  'GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE',\n  'METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY',\n  'SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY',\n]);\n\n// The subset a re-derive can actually settle, because they are assertions about\n// graph-metadata.json itself. The others describe description.json contents and\n// in-document reference paths, which a re-derive does not write; planning one\n// for them would be a write that changes nothing and a report line that never\n// clears.\nconst REDERIVABLE = new Set([\n  'GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY',\n  'GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT',\n  'GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE',\n  'METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY',\n]);\n\nconst POINTER_LINE = /^([ \\t]*packet_pointer:[ \\t]*)([\"']?)([^\"'\\r\\n]*)([\"']?)[ \\t]*\\r?$/m;\nconst SPEC_FOLDER_ROW = /(\\|[ \\t]*\\*\\*Spec Folder\\*\\*[ \\t]*\\|[ \\t]*)([^|\\r\\n]+?)([ \\t]*\\|)/;\nconst DOCS = ['spec.md', 'plan.md', 'tasks.md', 'implementation-summary.md', 'handover.md'];\nconst PACKET_MARKERS = new Set(['spec.md', 'implementation-summary.md']);\n\n// A marker alone is not enough: the metadata writer this script drives also\n// requires the numbered folder name, and handing it a folder it will refuse\n// turns a correctly out-of-scope directory into a reported failure. The two\n// definitions of \"packet\" have to agree or the failure count means nothing.\n// Mirrors SPEC_FOLDER_RE in backfill-graph-metadata.ts.\nconst PACKET_NAME_RE = /^\\d{3}(?:[-_].+)?$/;\n\n// The recorded location lives in the leading YAML block. A pointer written into\n// a document's body is an illustration of the format, not this packet's own\n// record, and rewriting it would corrupt the passage it explains. The block can\n// sit behind a template-source HTML comment, so the opener is matched past\n// leading comments and blank lines rather than demanded at byte zero. Every\n// repeat here consumes a newline, so the group cannot loop on an empty match.\nconst FRONTMATTER_OPEN = /^\\uFEFF?(?:[ \\t]*\\r?\\n|<!--[\\s\\S]*?-->[ \\t]*\\r?\\n)*---[ \\t]*\\r?\\n/;\nconst FRONTMATTER_CLOSE = /^(?:---|\\.\\.\\.)[ \\t]*\\r?$/m;\n\nconst USAGE = 'Usage: repair-derived.cjs [--folder <packet>]... [--roots <dir>] [--apply]';\n\n// Reported as one planned step like any other, so a dry run names it and the\n// exit code counts it. Carries no apply(): the re-derive is a child process the\n// repair awaits, not a file this tool writes itself.\nconst REDERIVE_STEP = Object.freeze({ what: 're-derive graph metadata' });\n\n/** Rejected arguments, kept apart from failures so the usage line follows them. */\nclass UsageError extends Error {}\n\nfunction fail(message) {\n  throw new UsageError(message);\n}\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 3. DIAGNOSIS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nfunction parseReport(stdout) {\n  try {\n    const report = JSON.parse(stdout);\n    return report && typeof report === 'object' ? report : null;\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\n// Exit 3 is the validator declining to run at all: a stale or missing runtime\n// build, or a folder it cannot find. It writes no report on that path, so its\n// stderr is the only account of why the packet could not be read.\nconst VALIDATOR_UNAVAILABLE = 3;\n\n/** The last lines of a child's stderr, joined for one report line. */\nfunction stderrTail(text, count = 3) {\n  return String(text || '').split('\\n').map((line) => line.trim()).filter(Boolean).slice(-count).join(' | ');\n}\n\n/** Why the validator declined to run, from the last lines of its stderr. */\nfunction validatorUnavailable(err) {\n  const label = `validator unavailable (exit ${VALIDATOR_UNAVAILABLE})`;\n  const tail = stderrTail(err.stderr);\n  return tail ? `${label}: ${tail}` : label;\n}\n\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"729fee","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_a92e9a11a09748a69f950bd3f7323751","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Generated Metadata Drift Gate\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// Re-derives one spec folder and compares the two stored synopsis fields against a fresh\n// derivation, so a description.json or graph-metadata.json that fell out of sync with the docs\n// it summarizes is provable rather than silently stale. The gate reads and reports only: it\n// never writes the folder, so it cannot churn the very files it exists to keep clean. Severity\n// resolution is left to the caller so the same check backs both the grandfather report rollout\n// and the enforced run. It pairs with source_doc_hashes, a cheap freshness key so a strict run\n// can skip the re-derive on a folder whose source docs are unchanged.\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nimport crypto from 'node:crypto';\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport { derivePacketSynopsis, } from '../description/packet-synopsis.js';\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n/** Validation rule id reported for the generated-metadata drift gate. */\nexport const GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT_RULE = 'GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT';\n// The packet docs whose content the synopsis can read. spec.md is the one the precedence\n// derives from; the rest round out an honest freshness key so any source edit moves a hash.\n// Conservative by design: a hash change that is not a synopsis change only triggers a re-derive,\n// it never hides one.\nconst SYNOPSIS_SOURCE_DOCS = [\n    'spec.md',\n    'plan.md',\n    'tasks.md',\n    'decision-record.md',\n    'implementation-summary.md',\n    path.join('research', 'research.md'),\n    'research.md',\n    'handover.md',\n    'resource-map.md',\n];\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 4. HELPERS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n/**\n * Hash the source docs the synopsis derives from, keyed by their packet-relative path.\n *\n * A doc edit changes its hash, giving the drift gate a cheap freshness key it can compare\n * before paying for a re-derive. Only present docs are hashed, so an absent doc carries no key\n * rather than a hash of empty content.\n *\n * @param folderPath - Absolute or relative path to the spec folder\n * @returns A map of relative doc path to sha256 hex digest for each present source doc\n */\nexport function computeSourceDocHashes(folderPath) {\n    const folder = path.resolve(folderPath);\n    const hashes = {};\n    for (const relativePath of SYNOPSIS_SOURCE_DOCS) {\n        const docPath = path.join(folder, relativePath);\n        let content;\n        try {\n            // A linked parent can expose another packet's source, so hash only local targets.\n            if (!isWithinPacketFolder(docPath, folder))\n                continue;\n            content = fs.readFileSync(docPath, 'utf-8');\n        }\n        catch {\n            continue;\n        }\n        hashes[relativePath.replace(/\\\\/g, '/')] = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(content).digest('hex');\n    }\n    return hashes;\n}\nfunction isWithinPacketFolder(filePath, packetFolderPath) {\n    try {\n        const realPacketFolderPath = fs.realpathSync(packetFolderPath);\n        const realFilePath = fs.realpathSync(filePath);\n        const relativePath = path.relative(realPacketFolderPath, realFilePath);\n        return relativePath === '' || (relativePath !== '..'\n            && !relativePath.startsWith(`..${path.sep}`)\n            && !path.isAbsolute(relativePath));\n    }\n    catch {\n        return false;\n    }\n}\nfunction readJsonObject(filePath) {\n    let raw;\n    try {\n        raw = fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf-8');\n    }\n    catch (error) {\n        const code = typeof error === 'object' && error && 'code' in error\n            ? String(error.code)\n            : null;\n        return { ok: false, reason: code === 'ENOENT' ? 'missing' : 'unreadable' };\n    }\n    try {\n        const parsed = JSON.parse(raw);\n        if (!parsed || typeof parsed !== 'object' || Array.isArray(parsed)) {\n            return { ok: false, reason: 'unparseable' };\n        }\n        return { ok: true, value: parsed };\n    }\n    catch {\n        return { ok: false, reason: 'unparseable' };\n    }\n}\nfunction readStoredCausalSummary(graph) {\n    const derived = graph.derived;\n    if (!derived || typeof derived !== 'object') {\n        return null;\n    }\n    const value = derived.causal_summary;\n    return typeof value === 'string' ? value : null;\n}\nfunction readStoredSourceDocHashes(graph) {\n    const derived = graph.derived;\n    if (!derived || typeof derived !== 'object') {\n        return null;\n    }\n    const value = derived.source_doc_hashes;\n    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object' || Array.isArray(value)) {\n        return null;\n    }\n    return value;\n}\nfunction hashMapsEqual(a, b) {\n    const aKeys = Object.keys(a).sort();\n    const bKeys = Object.keys(b).sort();\n    if (aKeys.length !== bKeys.length) {\n        return false;\n    }\n    return aKeys.every((key, index) => key === bKeys[index] && a[key] === b[key]);\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"111eb3","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_abb67f6acdbd45a38d9b90755d1d9481","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# COMPONENT: CHECK-AC-COVERAGE\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Sourced by validate.sh and compatible with strict mode.\nset -euo pipefail\n\n_ac_lower() {\n    printf '%s' \"$1\" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]'\n}\n\n# Only an explicit falsey value turns the gate off. Treating every unrecognized\n# value as \"off\" meant a typo silently disabled the check, which is the failure\n# an enable-flag should never have: a mistake should leave the gate running, not\n# quietly remove it.\n# The enforce switch promotes an under-floor result from advisory to a failing\n# rule; it defaults off so the floor stays a target, not a gate.\n_ac_enforce() {\n    local value\n    value=\"$(_ac_lower \"${SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE:-false}\")\"\n    [[ \"$value\" == \"true\" || \"$value\" == \"1\" || \"$value\" == \"yes\" || \"$value\" == \"on\" ]]\n}\n\n_ac_enabled() {\n    local value\n    value=\"$(_ac_lower \"${SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE:-true}\")\"\n    case \"$value\" in\n        false|0|no|off) return 1 ;;\n        *) return 0 ;;\n    esac\n}\n\n_ac_numeric_level() {\n    printf '%s' \"$1\" | tr -cd '0-9'\n}\n\n_ac_clamped_floor() {\n    local raw=\"${SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_FLOOR:-0.9}\"\n    awk -v raw=\"$raw\" 'BEGIN {\n        value = raw + 0\n        if (raw !~ /^[-+]?[0-9]*\\.?[0-9]+$/) value = 0.9\n        if (value < 0) value = 0\n        if (value > 1) value = 1\n        printf \"%.6f\", value\n    }'\n}\n\n_ac_floor_was_clamped() {\n    local raw=\"${SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_FLOOR:-0.9}\"\n    awk -v raw=\"$raw\" 'BEGIN {\n        if (raw !~ /^[-+]?[0-9]*\\.?[0-9]+$/) exit 0\n        value = raw + 0\n        exit(value < 0 || value > 1 ? 0 : 1)\n    }'\n}\n\n_ac_required_count() {\n    local total=\"$1\"\n    local floor=\"$2\"\n    awk -v total=\"$total\" -v floor=\"$floor\" 'BEGIN {\n        required = total * floor\n        rounded = int(required)\n        if (required > rounded) rounded += 1\n        print rounded\n    }'\n}\n\n# Rollout boundary for the enforce switch, the same shape the closure gate uses:\n# a packet created after the cutoff fails under the floor when enforcement is\n# on, a packet created on or before it stays advisory on every branch, and a\n# malformed override falls back to the default instead of grandfathering\n# everything by string comparison.\n_AC_CUTOFF_DEFAULT=\"2026-08-30\"\n_AC_CUTOFF_NOTE=\"\"\n_ac_coverage_cutoff_date() {\n    local raw=\"${SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_CUTOFF:-$_AC_CUTOFF_DEFAULT}\"\n    local candidate=\"${raw:0:10}\"\n    if [[ \"$candidate\" =~ ^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$ ]]; then\n        printf '%s' \"$candidate\"\n        return 0\n    fi\n    _AC_CUTOFF_NOTE=\"SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_CUTOFF='$raw' is not an ISO date; using $_AC_CUTOFF_DEFAULT\"\n    printf '%s' \"$_AC_CUTOFF_DEFAULT\"\n}\n\n# Packet creation date from the spec.md metadata table; the awk lowers the line\n# itself because IGNORECASE is not honoured on every platform.\n_ac_created_date() {\n    local spec_file=\"$1\"\n    [[ -f \"$spec_file\" ]] || return 1\n    local value\n    value=\"$(awk '\n        { line = tolower($0) }\n        line ~ /\\|[[:space:]]*\\*{0,2}created\\*{0,2}[[:space:]]*\\|/ {\n            if (match($0, /[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}/)) {\n                print substr($0, RSTART, RLENGTH)\n                exit\n            }\n        }\n    ' \"$spec_file\")\"\n    [[ -n \"$value\" ]] || return 1\n    printf '%s' \"$value\"\n}\n\n# True when the packet was created after the cutoff, so the enforce switch may\n# fail it. A packet with no readable creation date is treated as pre-cutoff.\n_ac_after_cutoff() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    local created cutoff\n    created=\"$(_ac_created_date \"$folder/spec.md\")\" || return 1\n    cutoff=\"$(_ac_coverage_cutoff_date)\"\n    [[ \"$created\" > \"$cutoff\" ]]\n}\n\n_ac_status_is_active() {\n    case \"$1\" in\n        in-progress|\"in progress\"|implemented|complete|completed|done|shipped|delivered) return 0 ;;\n    esac\n    return 1\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"de1520","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_b17d8c0a3c9b4c7ea4a50014817e136f","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-ac-coverage.sh:206:_ac_count_requirement_table() {\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-ac-coverage.sh:267:    _ac_count_requirement_table \"$spec_file\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/orchestrator.ts:785:    // demanding an anchored surface they never had is inventing a requirement.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"d7df0b","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_b3239c792a41456fb5f99446c084d7f7","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"[\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"FILE_EXISTS\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"FILES\",\n      \"FILES_PRESENT\",\n      \"FILES_EXISTS\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-files.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"PLACEHOLDER_FILLED\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"PLACEHOLDER\",\n      \"PLACEHOLDERS\",\n      \"PLACEHOLDERS_FILLED\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-placeholders.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Rejects unfilled template placeholders in authored spec documents.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"COMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"COMMENT_HYGIENE\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-comment-hygiene.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Rejects ephemeral finding markers inside HTML comments in authored spec documents.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"SCAFFOLD_MARKERS\",\n      \"TEMPLATE_SCAFFOLD\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-scaffold-never-touched.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Rejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"STATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"STATUS_CONSISTENCY\",\n      \"CROSS_DOC_STATUS\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-status-cross-doc-consistency.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Advisory-by-default check that spec.md and implementation-summary.md status fields classify to the same delivery state.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"LEVEL_DECLARED\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"LEVEL\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-level.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"info\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Reports whether the documentation level was declared or inferred.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"AC_COVERAGE\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"ACCEPTANCE_COVERAGE\",\n      \"AC_TRACEABILITY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-ac-coverage.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"info\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"flags\": [\n      \"SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE\",\n      \"SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE\",\n      \"SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_FLOOR\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Default-on advisory (non-blocking) scan for acceptance-criteria traceability coverage; set SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=false to opt out.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"AC_CLOSURE\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"ACCEPTANCE_CLOSURE\",\n      \"AC_GATE\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-ac-closure.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"flags\": [\n      \"SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE\",\n      \"SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Gates packet closure on acceptance-criteria.md at Levels 2, 3 and 3+; unmet criteria block a completion claim and a waiver must cite an ADR that exists. Packets created before the cutoff stay advisory.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"ANCHORS_VALID\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"ANCHOR\",\n      \"ANCHORS\",\n      \"ANCHOR_MATCHED\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"native:orchestrator\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks anchors in each spec doc whose template defines them, ignoring fenced code; a phase parent is exempt, and research/research.md and review/review-report.md are skipped as free-form workflow documents. Errors: a doc with no anchors, an anchor opened twice, never closed, closed but never opened, or closed more times than it is opened. Nesting is also an error: an anchor opened inside another, closed before it is opened, or closed while another is still open, though markers quoted in inline code are ignored by the nesting check; an adr-NNN anchor may hold adr-NNN-* anchors. Template order is not checked.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"MEMORY_BLOCK\",\n      \"FRONTMATTER_MEMORY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"ts:spec-doc-structure\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates canonical _memory continuity frontmatter blocks.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"MERGE_LEGALITY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"MERGE\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"ts:spec-doc-structure\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates generated merge payloads against target anchor shape.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"SUFFICIENCY\",\n      \"DOC_SUFFICIENCY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"ts:spec-doc-structure\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks implementation-summary sufficiency after save/write flows.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"CONTAMINATION\",\n      \"CROSS_ANCHOR\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"ts:spec-doc-structure\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Detects route/category mismatches before generated content is merged.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"POST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"FINGERPRINT\",\n      \"POST_SAVE\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"ts:spec-doc-structure\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Verifies post-save fingerprints for generated writes.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"TOC_POLICY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"TOC\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-toc-policy.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Enforces table-of-contents placement policy.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"AI_PROTOCOLS\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"AI_PROTOCOL\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-ai-protocols.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates AI execution protocol sections in high-governance specs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"COMPLEXITY_MATCH\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"COMPLEXITY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-complexity.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks declared level against content complexity signals.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"FOLDER_NAMING\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-folder-naming.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates numbered spec-folder naming conventions.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"FRONTMATTER_VALID\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"FRONTMATTER\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-frontmatter.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates YAML frontmatter structure and required semantic values.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"FRONTMATTER_VALUES\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"FRONTMATTER_VALUE_LIST\",\n      \"CONTEXT_TYPE_VALUES\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-frontmatter-values.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Warns when a packet document's contextType or importance_tier is outside the shared list in sk-doc/sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-values.json. Aliases are legal.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"SOURCE_TAGS\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"SOURCE_TAG_RESOLVER\",\n      \"SOURCE_CITATIONS\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-source-tags.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"flags\": [\n      \"SPECKIT_SOURCE_TAG_CUTOFF\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Warns when a path:line citation inside a [SOURCE: ...] tag in a packet's research or review artifacts names a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, using sk-doc's citation resolver. Packets created on or before the cutoff are skipped. A pass means the path and line exist, not that they support the claim.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GREP_CONVENTION\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"GREP\",\n      \"GREPPABLE\",\n      \"RETRIEVAL_CONVENTION\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-grep-convention.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks every markdown document in a spec folder against the greppable-corpus convention: frontmatter variant, trigger phrase quality, anchor grammar and naming.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"LEVEL_MATCH\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-level-match.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks required files match the declared documentation level.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"GRAPH_METADATA\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-graph-metadata.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks generated description and graph metadata are present.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"CHILD_DRIFT\",\n      \"GRAPH_CHILD_DRIFT\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-graph-metadata-child-drift.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids missing on-disk phase children the writer would add (advisory unless SPECKIT_CHILD_DRIFT_ENFORCE=true).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"CHILD_IDENTITY\",\n      \"GRAPH_CHILD_IDENTITY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-graph-metadata-child-identity.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"description\": \"Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids entries whose leading path identity is not the packet's own current identity (stale rename residue the refresh writer now prunes).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"GRAPH_SHAPE\",\n      \"GRAPH_METADATA_VALID\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-graph-metadata-shape.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates graph-metadata.json shape: required packet/derived blocks, last_active_child_id pointer integrity for phase parents.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"METADATA_DISK_CONSISTENCY\",\n      \"DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-metadata-disk-consistency.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"description\": \"Advisory-by-default check that description.json, graph-metadata.json, and continuity ids match the real on-disk spec-folder path.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"DESCRIPTION_SHAPE\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"DESC_SHAPE\",\n      \"DESCRIPTION_VALID\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-description-shape.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates description.json shape: required name/description/level keys present and well-typed.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"NORMALIZER_LINT\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"NORMALIZER\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-normalizer-lint.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Strict-only lint for duplicated runtime normalizer helpers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"DOC_INTEGRITY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-spec-doc-integrity.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Verifies inline markdown references resolve within spec docs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"TEMPLATE_SOURCE\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-template-source.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE provenance markers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-canonical-save-root-spec.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Ensures canonical saves include a root spec reference.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-canonical-save-source-docs.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Ensures canonical saves include source document references.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-canonical-save-lineage.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Ensures canonical save lineage metadata is present.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-canonical-save-packet-identity.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks canonical save packet identity normalization.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-canonical-save-description-graph-freshness.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks generated description/graph freshness for canonical saves.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"validation/continuity-freshness.ts\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"strict_only\": true,\n    \"description\": \"Strict-mode freshness check for continuity frontmatter. The rule reports warn by default and escalates to fail under SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE; the ceiling here has to allow that escalation, since a warn ceiling would silently cap it.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"GENERATED_METADATA\",\n      \"METADATA_INTEGRITY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"strict_only\": true,\n    \"description\": \"Validates description.json and graph-metadata.json through the shared schemas plus path-prefix and status-enum invariants, error under strict behind a grandfather report mode.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"METADATA_DRIFT\",\n      \"SYNOPSIS_DRIFT\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"validation/generated-metadata-drift.ts\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"strict_only\": true,\n    \"description\": \"Re-derives a folder and reports drift between the stored description/causal_summary and the current docs, read-only, error under strict only when the drift-gate flag is on and otherwise grandfather report mode.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"LINKS_VALID\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"WIKILINKS_VALID\",\n      \"CHECK_LINKS\"\n    ],\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Scans the system-spec-kit skill's own markdown for wikilinks whose target file does not exist. The target is always this skill, never the validated packet.\",\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-links.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\"\n  }\n]\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"8548b8","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_b38a4a5c4da84219b251bf6e6e34b88d","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"?? specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"9d86fb","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_bd681c3fd29b4a0cace5034267b3a068","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":" * doc set plus their non-volatile content decide the digest. Both the generator write and\n * the strict read go through this one function, so a fingerprint produced at write time and\n * one re-derived at validation time are comparable byte-for-byte.\n *\n * @param docs - The source docs to fingerprint, by packet-relative path and raw content\n * @returns A `sha256:`-prefixed hex digest of the volatile-ignoring projection\n */\n/**\n * Generation counter for the canonical source-doc set the fingerprint spans.\n *\n * Bump this whenever a document joins or leaves that set. Every stored digest then\n * reads as \"computed over an older set\" instead of as content drift, so a packet\n * nobody touched does not start failing validation because the toolchain changed\n * shape. Digests refresh naturally on the next save or repair.\n *\n * 2: the standalone verification checklist left the set; the merged tasks document\n *    carries its content.\n * 3: the acceptance-criteria and goal documents joined it - both decide packet\n *    state, and an unhashed document is an edit nobody detects.\n */\nexport const SOURCE_FINGERPRINT_DOCSET = 3;\n/** Compute the `sha256:`-prefixed source fingerprint over an already-collected set of packet docs. */\nexport function computeSourceFingerprintFromDocs(docs) {\n    const projected = docs\n        .map((doc) => projectDocForFingerprint(doc.relativePath, doc.content))\n        .sort((a, b) => (a[0] < b[0] ? -1 : a[0] > b[0] ? 1 : 0));\n    const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(JSON.stringify(projected)).digest('hex');\n    return `sha256:${hash}`;\n}\n/**\n * Re-derive the source fingerprint for a spec folder by reading its canonical docs.\n *\n * Used by the strict read path that has only a folder path. It reads the same canonical doc\n * set the generator reads, so the re-derived fingerprint matches the stored one when the\n * docs are unchanged and diverges when a source doc changed without a re-derive.\n *\n * @param specFolderPath - Absolute path to the packet/spec folder\n * @returns The `sha256:`-prefixed fingerprint over the current source docs\n */\nexport function computeSourceFingerprintForFolder(specFolderPath) {\n    const docs = collectPacketDocs(specFolderPath).docs.map((doc) => ({\n        relativePath: doc.relativePath,\n        content: doc.content,\n    }));\n    return computeSourceFingerprintFromDocs(docs);\n}\nfunction resolveSpecFolderPath(specFolderPath) {\n    const normalized = specFolderPath.replace(/\\\\/g, '/');\n    const explicit = extractSpecFolderFromGraphMetadataPath(path.join(normalized, GRAPH_METADATA_FILENAME));\n    if (explicit) {\n        return explicit;\n    }\n    const segments = normalized.split('/').filter(Boolean);\n    const specsIndex = segments.findIndex((segment) => segment === 'specs');\n    if (specsIndex >= 0 && specsIndex < segments.length - 1) {\n        return segments.slice(specsIndex + 1).join('/');\n    }\n    return path.basename(specFolderPath);\n}\nfunction resolveParentId(specFolder) {\n    const segments = specFolder.split('/').filter(Boolean);\n    if (segments.length < 2) {\n        return null;\n    }\n    const parentLeaf = segments[segments.length - 2] ?? '';\n    if (!isSpecLeafSegment(parentLeaf)) {\n        return null;\n    }\n    return segments.slice(0, -1).join('/');\n}\n/** Resolve the specs-root-relative children_ids for a spec folder from its on-disk phase children. */\nexport function resolveChildrenIds(specFolderPath, specFolder) {\n    // With the hardening flag on, the derived children resolve through the one shared\n    // listPhaseChildren enumeration that isPhaseParent also consumes, so the parent\n    // classification and the children list can no longer disagree on what a child is.\n    // With the flag off this is byte-identical to the previous direct readdir filter.\n    if (isGeneratorHardeningEnabled()) {\n        return listPhaseChildren(specFolderPath)\n            .map((child) => `${specFolder}/${child.name}`)\n            .sort();\n    }\n    try {\n        return fs.readdirSync(specFolderPath, { withFileTypes: true })\n            .filter((entry) => entry.isDirectory() && isSpecLeafSegment(entry.name))\n            .map((entry) => `${specFolder}/${entry.name}`)\n            .sort();\n    }\n    catch {\n        return [];\n    }\n}\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"1bc161","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
